  "title": "Checkerboard m-sequence-based c-VEP dataset from",
  "description": "A checkerboard m-sequence-based code-modulated visual evoked potential (c-VEP) EEG dataset recorded from 16 healthy participants. It was collected to evaluate how the spatial frequency of visual stimuli affects the performance and user experience of c-VEP-based brain-computer interfaces. Recordings used 16 EEG channels at 256 Hz, with eight stimulus conditions per participant and three runs each (two for training, one for testing).",
  "methods_description": "EEG was recorded from 16 channels at 256 Hz (standard_1005 montage, 50 Hz line frequency) while participants viewed checkerboard m-sequence stimuli. The dataset was recorded in a single session, with each condition stored as a separate session to match the MOABB structure. Each session contains three runs: two for training and one for testing. Binary events (0 and 1) were annotated with HED tags.",
